ecrets-file-key.ts","bridge/src/core/clients/web/admin-sign-ins.ts","bridge/src/core/clients/web/cookies.ts"],"failure_reason":null,"findings":[{"demoted":true,"demoted_from":"major","description":"[demoted to minor: no concrete failure scenario, so it cannot gate; reported as major by the reviewer] When any DCR agent is listed, an unauthenticated caller can repeatedly POST its public redirect URI to /oauth/reg. Registration explicitly requires no initial access token, and this adapter checks only whether the supplied redirect URIs match a listing before saving each newly generated client ID. The request path has no registration throttle or admission quota, and GrantsStore retains Client rows without a bounded lifecycle; unlisting an agent only makes those rows unusable. Consequently, repeated requests can grow the shared database indefinitely and consume the capacity needed for state ingestion, OAuth and lease renewal. The MCP read limiter does not apply to this route. Add bounded registration admission and a storage lifecycle for unused registrations, with coverage showing repeated anonymous registrations cannot create unbounded persistent records. This is the DCR flooding threat identified as T11 in the security design.","finding_id":"finding-f4e2ea5370b83353","lineage_id":"lin-027f4e903f504453","location":"bridge/src/core/clients/issuer/grants-adapter.ts:127","relevance":"current","resolution":"open","severity":"minor","source_local_id":"R001","title":"Bound public client registration before persisting new clients"}],"harness_id":"codex-cli-file-primary","run_id":"run-20261110-230343975-312e4ebf","runtime_outcome":"completed","schema_version":"1.0","started_at":"2026-11-10T23:06:16.7010528+00:00","summary":"Completed risk-based inspection of the frozen implementation, covering authentication and enrollment, connector transport and recovery, persistence and lease handling, MCP read contracts, secret handling, and host/CI wiring. Found one major issue: unauthenticated dynamic client registration can grow persistent storage without a bound. The controller's single declared governance verification command succeeded against the supplied digest. No tests or builds were run in this reviewer session. Deployment and live-agent/soak work are explicitly planned in the snapshot and were not treated as completed implementation.","target_digest":"69b5a1f046690cd6d3726008b76cedea649e02d5","termination_verified":true,"validation":"valid","verdict":"findings"}